            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0611" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-09T10:00:00+08:00">April 9, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 9—2:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. This office’s 81, April 6, 11 a.m.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d537-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Foreign Office states that it has this morning received a telegram from
                        Shansi authorities stating that the sieges of Linfen (Pingyang) and Hungtung
                        were raised on April 2 and 4, respectively. The foreign missionaries at
                        those places are “quite safe” and continued protection is being afforded
                        them.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Repeated to Peiping, Tientsin, Shanghai.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
